{
  "page": 5,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "NONCONVEX SCENARIO REACHABILITY",
      "bbox": [
        219.00900268554688,
        41.200374603271484,
        390.268798828125,
        50.106937408447266
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To satisfy the scenario constraints, we set θi = 0 ∀i such that scenario δ(j) ∈Ai for at least one",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        89.68023681640625,
        521.9948120117188,
        105.81340026855469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j ∈{1, ..., N}. To minimize the objective while respecting θ ∈[0, 1]m we set θi = 1 for all other",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        104.01470184326172,
        522.003173828125,
        119.12240600585938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ai. Therefore, R(θ) is the solution to (9), the union of cells Ai that contain one or more scenarios",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        120.73724365234375,
        521.9977416992188,
        132.9114227294922
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "δ(j). This is the minimum volume union of cells that contains all scenarios, δ(1), . . . , δ(N).",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        132.97784423828125,
        484.3642578125,
        144.82444763183594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We define a support scenario to be the first scenario, δ(j), in any cell Ai. While this set of",
      "bbox": [
        106.93698120117188,
        146.53082275390625,
        522.004150390625,
        159.2032470703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "support scenarios is not unique, it is irreducible. These scenarios represent the smallest set of",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        162.1737060546875,
        522.0000610351562,
        171.9264373779297
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reachable states that is possible without changing the solution to (9). This satisfies the conditions",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        175.72369384765625,
        522.0001220703125,
        185.47642517089844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "needed to obtain the number of support scenarios, s∗",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        186.73251342773438,
        317.8871154785156,
        199.0254364013672
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N. We calculate ϵ a-posteriori using (4) with s∗",
      "bbox": [
        313.6549987792969,
        186.73257446289062,
        518.1641235351562,
        201.44830322265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N",
      "bbox": [
        513.9320068359375,
        194.37091064453125,
        520.6508178710938,
        201.4483642578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and the number of optimization variables, d (the number of cells in our partition). If the obtained ϵ",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        202.647216796875,
        522.0010986328125,
        212.5745086669922
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "does not satisfy the necessary bounds, we iteratively increase the number of samples, N, and repeat",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        216.19622802734375,
        522.0008544921875,
        226.12351989746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the process. This reachability algorithm based on partition A1, ..., Am is described in Algorithm 1.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        229.7452392578125,
        520.0033569335938,
        241.30955505371094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Algorithm 1 : Scenario reachability through tiling",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        254.41973876953125,
        310.63641357421875,
        264.3033752441406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1: Input: Black-box transition function model Φ(t1; t0, x0, d); Random variables X0 and D; Par-",
      "bbox": [
        96.11499786376953,
        271.485107421875,
        521.9979248046875,
        283.0483703613281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tition dimension m; Batch size B; Confidence parameter β ∈(0, 1).",
      "bbox": [
        108.54498291015625,
        284.4232177734375,
        406.0932312011719,
        294.9613952636719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2: Output: θ1, ..., θm corresponding to union of cells Aj such that Aj ∈R(θ) iff θ = 0; Robust-",
      "bbox": [
        96.11495971679688,
        297.97222900390625,
        522.002197265625,
        310.1463928222656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ness against constraint violation ϵ.",
      "bbox": [
        108.54498291015625,
        312.13214111328125,
        258.062255859375,
        322.0594177246094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3: Initialize θj = 1",
      "bbox": [
        96.11497497558594,
        325.68115234375,
        181.99452209472656,
        337.00543212890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "4: while ϵ is large do",
      "bbox": [
        96.11497497558594,
        339.23114013671875,
        189.1399688720703,
        349.1584167480469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "5:",
      "bbox": [
        96.1149673461914,
        354.2718505859375,
        103.09082794189453,
        362.2878112792969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N = (B· number of iterations)",
      "bbox": [
        119.45396423339844,
        352.16925048828125,
        253.968505859375,
        362.7074279785156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "6:",
      "bbox": [
        96.11497497558594,
        367.82086181640625,
        103.09083557128906,
        375.8368225097656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for all i ∈{1, ..., N} do",
      "bbox": [
        119.4539794921875,
        365.71826171875,
        226.53196716308594,
        376.1800842285156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "7:",
      "bbox": [
        96.11495971679688,
        381.369873046875,
        103.0908203125,
        389.3858337402344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Take samples x0i ∼X0, di ∼D",
      "bbox": [
        130.36395263671875,
        379.26727294921875,
        271.4437255859375,
        391.20245361328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "8:",
      "bbox": [
        96.11497497558594,
        394.91888427734375,
        103.09083557128906,
        402.9348449707031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Evaluate δ(i) = ϕ(t1; t0, x0i, di)",
      "bbox": [
        130.36398315429688,
        389.46917724609375,
        270.5476379394531,
        404.1813049316406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "9:",
      "bbox": [
        96.114990234375,
        408.4688720703125,
        103.09085083007812,
        416.4848327636719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If δ(i) ∈Ai, then set θi = 0",
      "bbox": [
        130.36398315429688,
        402.4072570800781,
        250.80252075195312,
        418.3004455566406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "10:",
      "bbox": [
        91.63197326660156,
        422.01788330078125,
        103.09103393554688,
        430.0338439941406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "calculate ϵ using Equation 4 where s∗",
      "bbox": [
        119.45397186279297,
        418.1605224609375,
        285.9320983886719,
        430.4534606933594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N = |R(θ)| and d = m.",
      "bbox": [
        281.6999816894531,
        419.9152526855469,
        387.2652893066406,
        433.4464416503906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "11: return θ1, . . . , θm; ϵ",
      "bbox": [
        91.63201904296875,
        434.0751647949219,
        201.32911682128906,
        444.8282775878906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3.2. Radial Basis Functions (RBFs)",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        471.345703125,
        254.5637969970703,
        481.1529846191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We now turn to a method that allows nonconvexity in both parameters, θ and x. Unlike the method",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        489.7670593261719,
        522.0047607421875,
        499.6943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "proposed in Section 3.1, this method is not amenable to existing approaches, such as those presented",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        503.4916076660156,
        522.0001831054688,
        513.2443237304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in (Devonport and Arcak, 2020b; Devonport, 2023). In this approach, we construct g(x, θ) from a",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        516.8660888671875,
        522.0023193359375,
        526.7933959960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "finite set of RBFs. We define a RBF, f(x, µ, σ), to be a Gaussian function of x, µ, σ, such that",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        530.4150390625,
        500.32830810546875,
        540.3423461914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "f(x, µ, σ) = e",
      "bbox": [
        252.62303161621094,
        564.5950927734375,
        316.3816833496094,
        574.2824096679688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "−1",
      "bbox": [
        316.3780212402344,
        556.0655517578125,
        327.8123474121094,
        565.0181884765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2",
      "bbox": [
        324.1600036621094,
        562.4495849609375,
        327.81231689453125,
        567.7576904296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(x−µi)2",
      "bbox": [
        330.2040100097656,
        552.383544921875,
        357.185302734375,
        562.1016845703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "σ2",
      "bbox": [
        339.6189880371094,
        561.7215576171875,
        347.769287109375,
        569.0886840820312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i",
      "bbox": [
        343.9019775390625,
        566.8435668945312,
        346.5679931640625,
        572.1516723632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(10)",
      "bbox": [
        503.82598876953125,
        559.78662109375,
        522.0005493164062,
        569.5393676757812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where µ is the center of a RBF and σ is the width of a RBF. We take g to be",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        588.0660400390625,
        420.5277099609375,
        597.9933471679688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "g(x, θ) =",
      "bbox": [
        239.60198974609375,
        620.3130493164062,
        281.7096252441406,
        630.0003662109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "m",
      "bbox": [
        288.86798095703125,
        608.7156982421875,
        296.35986328125,
        615.7931518554688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
